# Rust
/target
**/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Node — key-build engine deps, e2e playwright
node_modules/

# Secrets — NEVER commit keys, seeds, or real test vectors
*.seed
*.key
*.pem
*.secret
secrets/
*vector*.local.*
.env
.env.*

# Runtime artifacts
chain-eos.watermark
# atmirror default output (CARs, blobs, state; receipts graduate to dockets/)
mirror-out/

# Research-lane draft staging (one-door). Drafts live untracked under docs/;
# an adopted finding graduates to docs/ or docs/architecture/ with its own
# STATUS ledger line (as did-autonomi-spec.md did). These pens also hold
# FOR-COUNSEL (legal) and founder-decision drafts (tokenomics, governance
# parameters, peg ratios) the builder must not publish unilaterally.
# Non-destructive: files stay on disk; `git add -f` to adopt a specific one.
docs/findings/
# docs/design/* (not docs/design/) so the exception below can re-include one
# file — git cannot un-ignore a file whose PARENT DIR is excluded.
docs/design/*
# ...except the shared non-value-state spec: it is the ONE canonical home both
# surfaces + Fable's pointers reference, and implementation reads from it. The
# rest of docs/design/ stays a deferred holding pen.
!docs/design/non-value-states.md
# ...and UI-LAW.md, the estate-wide confirmation laws (S26-0825 D1/D2): the
# sprint-closing receipt re-derives its needles in CI, so the file rides the
# repo like any other law. Everything else in docs/design/ stays a pen.
!docs/design/UI-LAW.md

# Relay / working drafts marked DO_NOT_COMMIT in the filename. The marker was
# the ONLY thing protecting these, and a filename is not an access control:
# before this rule, 17 such files plus a docs backup zip sat untracked but
# fully stageable in a public repo — one `git add -A` from publication.
# Matches the marker anywhere in the path so a rename keeps the protection.
# Non-destructive: files stay on disk; `git add -f` to adopt a specific one.
*DO_NOT_COMMIT*

# Local archives / backups — never publish a bundle by accident. Nothing
# matching these is tracked today, so the rule costs nothing; `git add -f`
# remains the escape hatch if a fixture archive is ever deliberately adopted.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
BACKUP_*

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
 
# Python bytecode 
__pycache__/ 
*.pyc
# third-party source snapshots: preserved for sponsor-mirroring, never republished
archive-staging/
.hubshots/
tools/ln-rail/node_modules/
e2e/.local-agent-profile/
